 Privacy Policy for ShadowReplay

Last updated: September 26, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how ShadowReplay accesses, uses, stores, processes, and shares user information.

1. Developer Information

Application name: ShadowReplay
 Developer: Sunny
 Contact email: sunny33871@gmail.com

If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how ShadowReplay handles information, please contact the developer using the email address above.

2. About ShadowReplay

ShadowReplay is a pose and facial-expression imitation game.

Users can capture or select a reference photo and then take another photo while recreating the reference pose or expression. The app analyzes the photos to calculate a similarity score.

Depending on the selected game mode, the analysis may include:

Body landmark positions
Body proportions
Joint angles and directions
Eye appearance
Eyebrow positions
Mouth shape
Smile appearance
Head position and direction

ShadowReplay also supports multiplayer challenges, result cards, image saving, and sharing.

3. Camera and Photo Access

ShadowReplay may request access to the device camera and photo library so that users can:

Capture reference photos
Capture imitation photos
Select reference photos from the device
Create comparison images and scorecards
Save result images to the device gallery
Share result images through other applications

Photos are primarily processed on the user’s device. ShadowReplay does not independently upload gameplay photos to a server operated by the developer.

A photo is saved to the device gallery only when the user requests that action or when the app creates and saves a result image.

When a user chooses to share an image, the image is sent to the application or service selected by the user. That third-party application or service processes the shared content according to its own privacy policy.

Users should avoid including confidential, personal, or sensitive information in gameplay photos.

4. Pose and Facial-Expression Analysis

ShadowReplay uses on-device analysis to detect and compare visual features.

Depending on the selected mode, the app may analyze:

Skeletal landmark positions
Body positioning
Body proportions
Joint angles
Facial landmarks
Eyes and eyebrows
Mouth shape and smile
Head direction

This analysis is used to calculate game scores and produce gameplay results.

ShadowReplay does not use pose or facial-expression analysis to identify a person, authenticate a person, or create a biometric identity profile.

5. Information Stored on the Device

ShadowReplay may store the following information locally on the user’s device:

Guest trial start time and remaining trial period
Sign-in status
Selected language
Game settings
Selected game mode
Multiplayer settings
Reference and participant photo locations
Gameplay scores and progress
Subscription status
Generated comparison images and scorecards

This information is used to operate the app, maintain game progress, remember preferences, and provide requested features.

Users can remove locally stored app data through the Android system settings. Uninstalling ShadowReplay may also remove locally stored app data, although photos or scorecards previously saved to the device gallery may remain until the user deletes them.

6. Google Sign-In

ShadowReplay may offer Google Sign-In as an optional sign-in method.

When a user chooses Google Sign-In, Google may provide the account information required to complete authentication, such as an account identifier and basic profile information.

ShadowReplay does not request, receive, or store the user’s Google Account password.

Google processes Google Sign-In information according to Google’s applicable terms and privacy policies.

